      "description": "Watch AFC Wimbledon vs Wigan Athletic highlights and goals from League One on ReFooty: Football Highlights Hub. Match played on August 30, 2026. A Gruelling Encounter at Plough Lane AFC Wimbledon and Wigan Athletic locked horns in a gritty League One battle that tested the resolve of both squads. Every inch of the pitch was contested as both sides searched for a decisive breakthrough in a highly physical encounter. Early Disruptions and Physical Play On August 30, 2026 , the match began with an early tactical shift for the hosts as Akeel Higgins was forced off in the 12th minute, replaced by Archie Harris . The opening period was defined more by the referee's whistle than goalmouth action. A string of yellow cards were handed out to Archie Harris , Jon Mellish , and Jensen Weir as the intensity threatened to boil over. Despite the high energy, neither side could find the clinical edge required to break the deadlock before the interval. Tactical Adjustments in the Second Half The second half saw a continuation of the physical theme, with James Carragher of Wigan Athletic entering the book in the 65th minute. As both managers turned to their benches to find a spark, AFC Wimbledon faced a period of heavy disciplinary pressure. In a frantic ten-minute spell, Steven Sessegnon , Ollie Harrison , and Alistair Smith were all cautioned. The match seemed to be drifting toward a stalemate as the clock ticked down and defensive lines remained resolute. Hippolyte Finds the Breakthrough The defining moment finally arrived in the 88th minute. Substitute Donnell McNeilly proved to be the difference-maker, delivering a perfect ball for Myles Hippolyte , who clinicaly finished to send the home fans into raptures. A marathon twelve minutes of stoppage time followed, during which Steve Seddon received a yellow card, but AFC Wimbledon remained organized at the back to see out the result and claim all three points."
